WEBVTT

00:00:01.910 --> 00:00:04.580
Osaka

00:00:05.230 --> 00:00:09.000
As I said, the master is currently away!

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:10.530
Insolent whelp!

00:00:11.330 --> 00:00:15.130
We are devoted warriors who have traveled

00:00:15.130 --> 00:00:18.850
all the way from the east to
fight for national loyalism!

00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:21.060
I am most sorry!

00:00:21.700 --> 00:00:23.030
I beg of you!

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:27.160
Please accept this and
pardon his insolence!

00:00:25.230 --> 00:00:27.940
Tempo
Koban of 50 Ryou

00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:30.300
What’s this?

00:00:31.030 --> 00:00:32.740
You were here after all.

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:37.330
Serizawa-san, what were you thinking?!

00:00:36.110 --> 00:00:39.950
Money Exchange House

00:00:37.640 --> 00:00:41.970
We came to Osaka to borrow
money to fund the Roshigumi!

00:00:42.550 --> 00:00:43.770
But you...

00:00:43.770 --> 00:00:46.310
Doesn’t this make us no better than the

00:00:46.310 --> 00:00:48.730
rogue samurai who forcibly borrow money?!

00:00:48.730 --> 00:00:53.030
In this day and age,
those who save easy money

00:00:53.030 --> 00:00:56.200
clearly made a profit by doing
business with foreigners.

00:00:56.500 --> 00:00:59.760
I would think that punishing
such vile merchants

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:02.630
is part of our duty as nationalists.

00:01:02.630 --> 00:01:04.400
You’re using fuzzy logic!

00:01:04.790 --> 00:01:08.620
Then do you know of
another way to procure

00:01:08.620 --> 00:01:10.000
funding for the Roshigumi?

00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:14.440
Serizawa-sensei is out here doing

00:01:14.440 --> 00:01:17.300
the dirty work to gather funds...

00:01:17.300 --> 00:01:19.260
What right do you have to criticize him

00:01:19.260 --> 00:01:21.140
when you haven’t done a thing?

00:01:22.270 --> 00:01:26.020
You can’t even play
the villain, can you?

00:01:26.270 --> 00:01:27.400
What?!

00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:29.170
A samurai’s existence must be

00:01:29.170 --> 00:01:31.520
awe-inspiring to the ordinary citizens.

00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:33.820
Moreover, you must be resolved

00:01:33.820 --> 00:01:36.530
to incite fear in the hearts of others

00:01:36.530 --> 00:01:38.720
if you intend to fight against the rogue

00:01:38.720 --> 00:01:40.030
samurai in the future.

00:01:40.790 --> 00:01:42.820
We need... resolve?

00:03:20.530 --> 00:03:22.560
Hijikata-san’s taking forever.

00:03:23.070 --> 00:03:25.850
This place is filled with nasty vibes.

00:03:26.480 --> 00:03:29.790
I think I’m going to take
a walk around the area.

00:03:36.020 --> 00:03:38.550
Nagakura-kun, handle things here.

00:03:46.850 --> 00:03:48.370
Is the boat ready yet?

00:03:49.530 --> 00:03:51.420
Should I go see how it’s coming along?

00:03:51.420 --> 00:03:54.050
Wait! Nagakura-kun, you may stay.

00:03:54.510 --> 00:03:55.580
Go on, dog!

00:03:55.580 --> 00:03:56.380
What?

00:03:58.450 --> 00:04:00.940
F-fine! I’ll go ask!

00:04:05.130 --> 00:04:08.150
Why does everyone always leave me behind?

00:04:08.890 --> 00:04:13.890
EPISODE 5:
Stairway to the Blue Skies

00:04:23.490 --> 00:04:24.500
Oh, it’s you.

00:04:24.720 --> 00:04:25.590
What is it?

00:04:25.590 --> 00:04:28.660
Serizawa-san wants to know
when the boat is departing.

00:04:30.290 --> 00:04:31.960
Apparently there was
some sort of mistake,

00:04:31.960 --> 00:04:34.360
so it’s won’t be for a little while.

00:04:34.560 --> 00:04:35.580
Got it.

00:04:39.560 --> 00:04:40.920
I wonder why...

00:04:42.810 --> 00:04:45.980
I can’t stand a thing he says or does,

00:04:46.320 --> 00:04:48.600
but for some reason that

00:04:48.600 --> 00:04:51.180
man’s words stab deep into my chest.

00:04:51.780 --> 00:04:55.770
He makes me realize just
how naïve we have been.

00:05:00.230 --> 00:05:04.130
Say, this has been eating
at me this whole time...

00:05:06.130 --> 00:05:08.200
Have you spoken to Okita
since that incident?

00:05:08.950 --> 00:05:10.640
Haven’t you and Okita been

00:05:10.640 --> 00:05:12.950
pals since your dojo days in Edo?

00:05:18.330 --> 00:05:20.040
I don’t need to worry about

00:05:20.040 --> 00:05:22.960
Souji with Kondou-san dealing with him.

00:05:22.960 --> 00:05:23.710
But--!

00:05:27.260 --> 00:05:28.210
It’s nothing...

00:05:31.700 --> 00:05:33.130
Maybe I should go.

00:05:33.850 --> 00:05:37.810
We can’t stay stuck like this forever.

00:05:43.380 --> 00:05:45.840
Several Days Later, Kyoto

00:05:48.360 --> 00:05:49.870
Ink Sticks

00:05:53.430 --> 00:05:54.640
Excuse me!

00:05:54.640 --> 00:05:56.250
I was asked to get an ink stick.

00:05:56.250 --> 00:05:57.370
Could you show me what you’ve got?

00:05:59.010 --> 00:06:00.380
I do not have any.

00:06:00.640 --> 00:06:02.430
Huh? You don’t?

00:06:02.830 --> 00:06:04.880
But doesn’t this shop
specialize in selling ink?

00:06:05.270 --> 00:06:06.760
That is correct,

00:06:06.760 --> 00:06:09.390
but I have already
sold out of today’s stock.

00:06:09.890 --> 00:06:12.000
Please take your leave.

00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:13.320
What?!

00:06:13.320 --> 00:06:15.060
There’s no way in the world

00:06:15.060 --> 00:06:17.060
you could have totally run out!

00:06:17.060 --> 00:06:19.060
Say what you will, but...

00:06:20.340 --> 00:06:21.970
My apologies, Sir.

00:06:21.970 --> 00:06:24.300
This man is an acquaintance of mine.

00:06:24.300 --> 00:06:25.070
Huh?

00:06:25.070 --> 00:06:27.030
Could you sell him a stick?

00:06:28.780 --> 00:06:30.840
Is that right?

00:06:30.840 --> 00:06:34.910
Come to think of it, I
just might have one left.

00:06:37.160 --> 00:06:38.660
Dried Blue Ink Stick

00:06:47.600 --> 00:06:49.140
I owe you one!

00:06:49.140 --> 00:06:50.270
Thanks a lot!

00:06:50.820 --> 00:06:51.670
It’s nothing.

00:06:52.750 --> 00:06:54.930
There are some in Kyoto who feel uneasy

00:06:54.930 --> 00:06:57.090
when they hear your eastern dialect.

00:06:57.090 --> 00:06:58.500
Please don’t hold it against him.

00:06:58.830 --> 00:07:01.600
Ah, so that’s what the deal was.

00:07:02.760 --> 00:07:06.440
By the way, have I met
you somewhere before?

00:07:09.190 --> 00:07:12.220
I see elite samurai do
not remember everything

00:07:12.220 --> 00:07:13.950
that happens in a banquet room.

00:07:14.310 --> 00:07:15.240
Huh?

00:07:19.500 --> 00:07:21.210
Thank you for your help back then.

00:07:26.410 --> 00:07:28.960
Oh, it’s you!

00:07:29.380 --> 00:07:32.570
I totally didn’t recognize
you without your MAIKO attire!

00:07:33.940 --> 00:07:35.720
How was your injury?

00:07:37.120 --> 00:07:38.890
The doctor say that it
merely gave me a bump,

00:07:38.890 --> 00:07:43.840
so I may return to work once
it isn’t so noticeable.

00:07:44.590 --> 00:07:45.460
I see...

00:07:46.090 --> 00:07:47.730
It must have been a nightmare.

00:07:49.780 --> 00:07:52.080
I have heard that the
man named Serizawa-han

00:07:52.080 --> 00:07:56.730
came to Kyoto with the
Roshigumi to protect Kyoto.

00:07:56.730 --> 00:07:58.630
Uh, r-right...

00:07:59.290 --> 00:08:02.940
Then why does he treat the weak

00:08:02.940 --> 00:08:04.750
such as myself so cruelly?

00:08:05.070 --> 00:08:08.500
N-no, it isn’t limited to the weak!

00:08:08.910 --> 00:08:11.650
He’s always mean to me and the

00:08:11.650 --> 00:08:13.680
members of the Roshigumi.

00:08:15.030 --> 00:08:15.940
Uh-huh!

00:08:22.580 --> 00:08:25.470
Yeah, but seriously, why
did you talk back to him?

00:08:25.470 --> 00:08:26.020
Huh?

00:08:26.820 --> 00:08:29.470
I mean, considering
where you work and all,

00:08:29.470 --> 00:08:31.780
shouldn’t you act a
bit more businesslike?

00:08:33.990 --> 00:08:36.530
What do you mean by “considering
where I work”?

00:08:37.260 --> 00:08:41.220
Huh? Well, don’t you
get paid for serving SAKE

00:08:41.220 --> 00:08:43.660
and casually pleasing your customers?

00:08:50.680 --> 00:08:53.100
You don’t know anything about me,

00:08:53.100 --> 00:08:54.930
so don’t make that stuff up!

00:08:55.210 --> 00:08:56.180
H-hey, wait!

00:09:13.800 --> 00:09:15.850
Yo! If it isn’t Ryunosuke!

00:09:15.850 --> 00:09:16.960
What’s up?

00:09:20.140 --> 00:09:21.320
You moron!

00:09:23.050 --> 00:09:24.650
What was that for?!

00:09:24.650 --> 00:09:27.830
You actually said that crap
to that nice little MAIKO?

00:09:28.320 --> 00:09:31.590
No wonder she gave you that handprint.

00:09:34.340 --> 00:09:35.720
Unbelievable... We’re going.

00:09:36.750 --> 00:09:38.320
Go? Go where?

00:09:38.790 --> 00:09:42.100
You’re gonna go apologize
to that little lady, duh!

00:09:42.100 --> 00:09:43.730
Ow, ow! Why should I?!

00:09:43.730 --> 00:09:44.750
Just apologize!

00:09:44.750 --> 00:09:46.190
Wait, wait! That hurts!

00:09:46.190 --> 00:09:47.100
Come on, moron!

00:09:47.100 --> 00:09:50.610
Shimabara

00:09:47.600 --> 00:09:50.610
Hey, mind if I ask you something?

00:09:50.790 --> 00:09:52.650
We’re searching for a MAIKO.

00:09:52.650 --> 00:09:55.150
Okay. What is the girl’s name?

00:09:55.760 --> 00:09:57.160
Ryunosuke?

00:09:57.990 --> 00:10:00.690
Like I said, I’m not apolo--Ow!

00:10:00.690 --> 00:10:03.890
Be good and answer the question!

00:10:03.890 --> 00:10:05.330
What’s her name?

00:10:05.820 --> 00:10:07.370
Pretty sure it’s Kosuzu.

00:10:07.370 --> 00:10:10.060
Oh, if you’re looking
for Kosuzu-chan...

00:10:14.320 --> 00:10:16.380
No, no! Stop, stop!

00:10:16.380 --> 00:10:19.790
Kosuzu, how many times must I tell you?

00:10:19.860 --> 00:10:22.860
Did I not tell you to slowly
turn to the right at that part?

00:10:22.860 --> 00:10:24.690
You did. I apologize.

00:10:24.690 --> 00:10:27.220
Mother, please let me try again.

00:10:29.720 --> 00:10:32.390
Okay. Turn there and bow.

00:10:33.150 --> 00:10:35.150
Right. Be sure to bow low.

00:10:35.430 --> 00:10:37.660
She is currently in the
middle of practice...

00:10:37.660 --> 00:10:39.090
Do it again!
Okay. Then we’ll wait here for a bit.

00:10:39.090 --> 00:10:40.160
Okay!
Okay. Then we’ll wait here for a bit.

00:10:41.330 --> 00:10:44.270
Okay, now turn and bow.

00:10:45.060 --> 00:10:46.160
Right.

00:10:47.230 --> 00:10:48.910
Thank you kindly.

00:10:51.030 --> 00:10:53.800
Ma’am, there is a customer
here to see Kosuzu-han.

00:10:56.590 --> 00:10:58.150
Sorry for the wait.

00:10:59.680 --> 00:11:01.000
Sorry to disturb ya.

00:11:01.260 --> 00:11:04.100
Apparently he said some
pretty rude stuff to you,

00:11:04.100 --> 00:11:05.680
so he came to apologize.

00:11:05.680 --> 00:11:07.230
Do it, Ryunosuke!

00:11:08.830 --> 00:11:10.000
Fine!

00:11:10.230 --> 00:11:12.350
Bowing in apology means nothing if

00:11:12.350 --> 00:11:14.440
he does not regret what he said.

00:11:14.900 --> 00:11:16.200
You’ve got a point.

00:11:16.930 --> 00:11:19.870
Sorry, but could you explain to

00:11:19.870 --> 00:11:23.050
this idiot why you got so mad?

00:11:23.050 --> 00:11:26.100
He’s truly an ignorant idiot!

00:11:26.100 --> 00:11:27.450
Quit calling me an idiot.

00:11:29.360 --> 00:11:32.820
Ibuki-han, you said
that we should casually

00:11:32.820 --> 00:11:35.680
try to please our banquet guests,

00:11:36.230 --> 00:11:38.560
but since arriving in Kyoto,

00:11:38.560 --> 00:11:41.420
I have not missed a single day of dance,

00:11:41.420 --> 00:11:43.660
SHAMISEN or music lessons.

00:11:46.270 --> 00:11:48.250
And not just me.

00:11:48.250 --> 00:11:50.270
The same is true of the other women.

00:11:51.370 --> 00:11:55.740
This place has been soaked
with our sweat and tears.

00:11:57.200 --> 00:11:59.090
All of us live by selling the arts

00:11:59.090 --> 00:12:02.460
we have worked so hard to master!

00:12:08.400 --> 00:12:09.550
I...

00:12:10.270 --> 00:12:11.730
Now do you get it?

00:12:12.070 --> 00:12:15.900
Everyone has something that
they will stand up for.

00:12:18.070 --> 00:12:19.670
I’m really sorry!

00:12:22.580 --> 00:12:24.120
I said something horrible

00:12:24.120 --> 00:12:27.150
when I didn’t know a thing about you!

00:12:27.150 --> 00:12:28.370
I’m sorry!

00:12:31.270 --> 00:12:32.980
That is enough.

00:12:32.980 --> 00:12:35.230
Please raise your head, Ibuki-han.

00:12:37.560 --> 00:12:40.040
I am sorry I slapped you.

00:12:40.040 --> 00:12:41.530
Are you all right?

00:12:42.200 --> 00:12:44.280
Uh, yeah, I guess...

00:12:44.280 --> 00:12:46.240
Although I was surprised
when it came out of nowhere.

00:12:51.840 --> 00:12:53.870
If you do not mind, could you ask for me

00:12:53.870 --> 00:12:56.380
the next time you visit a banquet room?

00:12:56.380 --> 00:12:58.200
Huh? But...

00:12:59.070 --> 00:13:02.170
There’s no way I’ll
get to visit one again.

00:13:03.210 --> 00:13:05.930
Please watch me perform my arts.

00:13:06.070 --> 00:13:08.250
No, like I said--

00:13:08.250 --> 00:13:10.130
Sheesh! Just say, “Okay!” already!

00:13:10.710 --> 00:13:12.670
What gives?! Let go of me!

00:13:12.670 --> 00:13:14.010
Be a man!

00:13:16.810 --> 00:13:17.860
Everyone, listen to this!

00:13:18.210 --> 00:13:20.700
We have been granted an audience

00:13:20.700 --> 00:13:23.180
with the lieutenant
general of Aizu tomorrow.

00:13:23.180 --> 00:13:25.300
All of the Roshigumi will visit

00:13:25.300 --> 00:13:27.820
the Kyoto Military
Commissioner’s headquarters.

00:13:27.820 --> 00:13:29.090
Awesome!

00:13:29.090 --> 00:13:31.750
That means they’ve finally
acknowledged how cool we are!

00:13:32.140 --> 00:13:33.890
What should I do?

00:13:33.890 --> 00:13:36.370
Y’know, I don’t have a thing to wear!

00:13:36.370 --> 00:13:38.140
Men, calm down!

00:13:38.140 --> 00:13:40.140
He’s not done talking!

00:13:40.600 --> 00:13:41.810
So here’s the deal:

00:13:41.810 --> 00:13:44.010
Since we will be in the presence of the

00:13:44.010 --> 00:13:45.880
Aizu Domain’s lieutenant general,

00:13:46.320 --> 00:13:49.390
I would like to hold some
matches for him to watch!

00:13:49.830 --> 00:13:51.220
Some matches for him?

00:13:51.220 --> 00:13:54.140
You mean we get to fight
in front of a lord?

00:13:54.320 --> 00:13:56.900
Yeah! It’d be a waste if we just

00:13:56.900 --> 00:13:59.900
went to meet him and ended at that.

00:14:00.110 --> 00:14:03.280
Why should we go through
all of that trouble?

00:14:03.540 --> 00:14:04.810
Indeed!

00:14:04.810 --> 00:14:08.160
The Aizu Domain hardly even
cough up money to fund our work.

00:14:08.490 --> 00:14:11.680
Leave all of that sweaty work to us.

00:14:12.160 --> 00:14:15.660
This job isn’t big enough
to concern two chiefs over it.

00:14:17.680 --> 00:14:19.790
We’ve already decided
who will face who.

00:14:20.920 --> 00:14:23.300
The first match will be
between Heisuke and I.

00:14:24.260 --> 00:14:26.300
I-I’m fighting Hijikata-san...?

00:14:26.580 --> 00:14:29.360
And the second match will be
between Shinpachi and Saito.

00:14:29.360 --> 00:14:30.980
Saito, eh?

00:14:30.980 --> 00:14:33.560
This should make for
a pretty interestin’ match!

00:14:33.830 --> 00:14:36.230
The final match will be
between Sannan-san and...

00:14:36.230 --> 00:14:38.990
...Souji, you.

00:14:41.590 --> 00:14:45.050
The Aizu Domain’s
assessment of us depends

00:14:45.050 --> 00:14:47.320
on the skills displayed in the matches,

00:14:47.680 --> 00:14:50.210
so please put your heart your practice!

00:14:50.210 --> 00:14:51.330
Yessir!

00:14:56.220 --> 00:14:58.070
Everyone’s all excited, huh?

00:14:58.070 --> 00:15:00.990
That’s because we finally
get our chance to shine.

00:15:02.290 --> 00:15:05.070
Oh, right! Ikubi-kun, why don’t you

00:15:05.070 --> 00:15:06.920
take advantage of this opportunity

00:15:06.920 --> 00:15:08.330
to start training with the sword?

00:15:08.330 --> 00:15:09.090
Me?!

00:15:09.290 --> 00:15:12.090
Yeah! I’d be willing to
personally instruct you.

00:15:12.390 --> 00:15:14.760
I-I’ll pass.

00:15:14.760 --> 00:15:17.380
I mean, with those important
matches coming up

00:15:17.380 --> 00:15:19.920
shouldn’t you overlook
everyone’s training instead?

00:15:20.250 --> 00:15:21.420
You think?

00:15:21.420 --> 00:15:23.050
In that case, I might do just that.

00:15:25.520 --> 00:15:26.990
What’s this?

00:15:26.990 --> 00:15:28.420
And here I thought you were going

00:15:28.420 --> 00:15:30.200
to refuse ’cause
“it’d be a hassle.”

00:15:30.200 --> 00:15:32.740
You’ve matured a bit, haven’t ya?

00:15:32.740 --> 00:15:34.370
Hey, knock it off!

00:15:34.370 --> 00:15:37.080
Headquarters of the Kyoto Military Commissioner
Konkaikoumyouji Main Temple

00:15:40.920 --> 00:15:43.770
Kondou-kun, I take it the men from your

00:15:43.770 --> 00:15:46.790
dojo will put on a show worth watching.

00:15:47.060 --> 00:15:50.050
I am confident that they will.

00:15:52.190 --> 00:15:54.290
You may now begin!

00:16:01.750 --> 00:16:03.100
What’s he doing?

00:16:03.370 --> 00:16:05.670
It’s called the “Wagtail Sword.”

00:16:05.670 --> 00:16:07.480
He keeps the sword constantly moving

00:16:07.480 --> 00:16:10.310
so that his opponent cannot
read when he will strike.

00:16:51.300 --> 00:16:54.680
Dang it! And here I was so close.

00:16:54.680 --> 00:16:56.580
Oh, Heisuke...

00:16:56.580 --> 00:16:57.650
Huh?

00:16:57.650 --> 00:17:00.290
Forget it. That was a good match.

00:17:03.430 --> 00:17:04.290
Begin!

00:17:06.320 --> 00:17:09.260
Isn’t that man’s stance backwards?

00:17:09.620 --> 00:17:12.300
Right, he is left-handed.

00:17:12.680 --> 00:17:14.650
Aren’t you going to make
him learn the right way?

00:17:14.650 --> 00:17:18.050
There are essentially no
left-handed warriors out there.

00:17:18.430 --> 00:17:21.220
In other words, there are no sword

00:17:21.220 --> 00:17:24.320
techniques to counter
a left-handed opponent.

00:17:25.100 --> 00:17:28.170
Nothing could be more
advantageous in actual combat.

00:17:28.410 --> 00:17:30.070
That makes sense.

00:17:40.780 --> 00:17:42.730
Most impressive, Saito!

00:17:42.730 --> 00:17:44.920
Have you improved some more?

00:17:44.920 --> 00:17:46.420
You have as well.

00:17:48.650 --> 00:17:51.170
But I’m going to win with my next move.

00:17:51.890 --> 00:17:54.220
I do not intend to lose!

00:18:15.390 --> 00:18:16.330
Stop there!

00:18:18.600 --> 00:18:20.860
His movement was amazing!

00:18:21.660 --> 00:18:24.150
Dammit! I lost.

00:18:24.150 --> 00:18:25.750
Good job!

00:18:27.000 --> 00:18:28.750
Is that the Wagtail Sword again?

00:18:28.750 --> 00:18:29.990
Yeah.

00:18:29.990 --> 00:18:31.670
But Sannan-san...

00:18:31.670 --> 00:18:33.750
Is that going to work on Souji?

00:18:40.260 --> 00:18:42.260
I can read your moves, Sannan-san.

00:18:43.760 --> 00:18:47.270
I see you’ve grown strong, Okita-kun.

00:18:47.850 --> 00:18:51.920
Souji’s stance has
changed a bit after all.

00:18:54.020 --> 00:18:57.760
I’m going to wrap this up, Sannan-san!

00:19:02.570 --> 00:19:05.530
Thanks to all of you, the
Aizu lieutenant general

00:19:05.530 --> 00:19:08.540
gave us wonderful words of praise.

00:19:08.820 --> 00:19:10.190
We’re partying today!

00:19:10.480 --> 00:19:11.860
Drink as much as you like!

00:19:21.730 --> 00:19:24.520
Hey, you guzzlin’ the booze, Ryunosuke?

00:19:24.520 --> 00:19:25.560
Not a sip.

00:19:25.800 --> 00:19:28.630
What, you can’t drink?

00:19:28.630 --> 00:19:33.090
Isn’t that bad for a warrior
who speaks of politics?

00:19:33.090 --> 00:19:34.770
Dude, that’s Niimi-san!

00:19:34.770 --> 00:19:36.570
You sounded just like him.

00:19:40.350 --> 00:19:42.650
When they get like this,
they won’t stop until morning,

00:19:42.650 --> 00:19:45.080
so you should turn in for
the day before too long.

00:19:45.350 --> 00:19:46.270
Yeah...

00:19:47.150 --> 00:19:49.630
Everyone’s psyched that the lord from

00:19:49.630 --> 00:19:51.580
Aizu complemented them, aren’t they?

00:19:51.780 --> 00:19:53.000
Yes.

00:19:53.000 --> 00:19:55.270
After all, it just increased the chances

00:19:55.270 --> 00:19:57.840
of Aizu becoming our patron.

00:19:58.840 --> 00:20:01.550
But the real trials are yet to come...

00:20:06.830 --> 00:20:08.850
Awesome! Too cool!

00:20:11.250 --> 00:20:13.290
So that’s our new uniform, eh?

00:20:13.290 --> 00:20:14.230
Yeah!

00:20:15.960 --> 00:20:18.820
In order to spread the Roshigumi’s
name throughout Kyoto,

00:20:18.820 --> 00:20:20.630
Serizawa-sensei had these made

00:20:20.630 --> 00:20:22.740
with the money he collected in Osaka.

00:20:22.920 --> 00:20:26.450
Hey, let’s go ahead and try ’em on!

00:20:26.450 --> 00:20:27.990
Would that be okay, Serizawa-san?

00:20:28.210 --> 00:20:29.630
Sure, go ahead!

00:20:29.630 --> 00:20:30.750
Try them on.

00:20:30.750 --> 00:20:32.500
Sweet!

00:20:33.120 --> 00:20:34.830
Gen-san, get the scissors! The scissors!

00:20:34.830 --> 00:20:35.900
We gotta cut off the tacking thread!

00:20:35.900 --> 00:20:36.710
Just give me a moment.

00:20:36.710 --> 00:20:38.240
Hurry! Hurry!

00:20:38.240 --> 00:20:40.000
I’ll cut it for you, so
sit still for a moment!

00:20:40.000 --> 00:20:41.130
Mine, too!

00:20:41.130 --> 00:20:43.560
Sano-san, what do you
think of these coats?

00:20:43.560 --> 00:20:45.950
I think they’re a bit flashy...

00:20:45.950 --> 00:20:47.430
Right, Saito?

00:20:47.430 --> 00:20:48.640
You have a point.

00:20:48.640 --> 00:20:51.840
This is one way to spread word about the

00:20:51.840 --> 00:20:53.890
Roshigumi throughout Kyoto.

00:20:55.250 --> 00:20:59.260
Besides, if we’re all in the same
uniform when we go on patrol,

00:20:59.260 --> 00:21:01.400
no one will confuse us
with those rogue samurai

00:21:01.860 --> 00:21:04.560
and it prevents us from accidentally
cutting down one of our own.

00:21:04.560 --> 00:21:05.910
Makes sense.

00:21:07.330 --> 00:21:09.920
Serizawa-san, do you have a moment?

00:21:10.780 --> 00:21:13.240
Henceforth, we may receive

00:21:13.240 --> 00:21:16.320
numerous opportunities
to guard Aizu’s elite.

00:21:16.320 --> 00:21:19.420
In which case, recruiting more men
will be a matter of great urgency.

00:21:20.530 --> 00:21:23.820
We already thought of that
and came up with a plan to--

00:21:25.150 --> 00:21:27.240
As long as we sell the
Roshigumi’s name,

00:21:27.240 --> 00:21:29.660
soldiers will come flocking to us.

00:21:29.660 --> 00:21:31.310
That’s what these uniforms are for.

00:21:31.740 --> 00:21:32.750
Hijikata!

00:21:41.800 --> 00:21:43.820
Okay, guys,

00:21:44.640 --> 00:21:45.700
let’s go!

00:21:45.700 --> 00:21:46.700
Yeah!

00:23:30.120 --> 00:23:31.550
The Shogunate ordered us to do this!

00:23:31.950 --> 00:23:33.050
Run for it, Ryunosuke!

00:23:33.530 --> 00:23:36.210
The way he looked...
He was definitely a Fury.

00:23:36.210 --> 00:23:38.330
If you lack any real resolve,

00:23:38.330 --> 00:23:40.140
don’t waltz out onto a battlefield.

00:23:41.400 --> 00:23:43.400
NEXT EPISODE:
Howling from the Darkness
